<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Open a P2P Lobby with another user: a single persistent peer-to-peer connection that hosts every feature at once — an audio or video call, file transfers, and games — all running at the same time."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_code}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Syntax")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/p2p <nickname>")}</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tag}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Parameters")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <code>nickname</code> {dgettext("help_commands", "— The user to open a P2P Lobby with.")}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_commands", "How It Works")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext("help_commands", "Running")} <code>{dgettext("help_commands", "/p2p")}</code>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "creates a lobby and sends the other user a join invitation. Once both of you join, one WebRTC connection is established and stays open. A dock lets either side start audio/video, send files, or propose a game at any time — and several can run together concurrently. Ending one activity keeps the connection alive; the lobby only closes when someone leaves or it goes idle."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Rules & Limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Both you and the target must be registered and identified (via")} <code>{dgettext("help_commands", "/ns identify")}</code>).
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "The target must be online.")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "You cannot open a lobby with yourself.")}</li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_commands", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-universal-lobby">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "P2P Lobby")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="feature-video-call">{dgettext("help_commands", "Video Call")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-file-transfer">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "File Transfer")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
